            <ArticleTitle>Cryosurgery of varicose veins.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>56-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">It is impossible to treat all varicose veins employing the same method. Cryosurgery offers a new modality for the detraction of the long and short saphenous vein deletion.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To describe the technique, its indications, potential complications, and cosmetic results.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We followed 800 patients over 6 years. The study allows evaluation of the results of and the best indications for this method. With a follow up of five years, we have analyzed: 1) the immediate complications, and 2) middle-term results.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The results of cryosurgery of varicose veins were generally comparable to those obtained using classical surgery (stripping).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Cryosurgery of varicose veins is a fast and safe method for selected varicose disorders, exhibiting good cosmetic results.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
